happen, anything possible

00:12:03.227 --> 00:12:05.660
until the world changes.
- Until the world changes?

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:06.493
- Mm-hm.

00:12:06.493 --> 00:12:09.160
- [Mark] What needs to
change with the world?

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:10.410
- Till the world changes.

00:12:13.640 --> 00:12:16.020
- [Mark] The world seems to be
changing a lot right, lately.

00:12:16.020 --> 00:12:17.453
- Real bad, quick.

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:22.203
I've seen so much out
there, it'd blow your mind.

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:26.870
But I stay, like, I don't
let that get in my way.

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:30.200
I just tell them, like, well,
it ain't gonna be me today,

00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:31.613
and that's all that I...

00:12:32.522 --> 00:12:33.355
You know what I'm saying?

00:12:33.355 --> 00:12:36.950
And I just keep on
going along with my day.

00:12:36.950 --> 00:12:40.100
And, like, yeah, I'm not an easy person,

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:43.170
but I'm not a hard person,

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:44.970
but I've been through hell and back.

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:48.200
How I've lived, I'll never know.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:50.830
- [Mark] I'd love to see who
you were 10, 15, 20 years ago.

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:51.750
- You can go back.

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:53.930
- [Mark] And I'd love to
see you go back there again.

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:54.880
- Yeah, I can allow you to go back.

00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:56.543
- [Mark] Get close to that.

00:12:56.543 --> 00:12:58.230
- You can go back and
review those records,

00:12:58.230 --> 00:13:00.860
everybody else has,
pretty much, in schools.

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:03.730
So you can, that's what I like about you,

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:06.980
is because you would always
ask, you know what I'm saying?

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:09.360
That's such a good thing,

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:12.130
because I feel like everything's
been stripped from me.

00:13:12.130 --> 00:13:15.480
They went all the way back
to where I used to live

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:20.230
in the hospital 24 hours
a day all the time,

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:24.380
I never would hardly go home
because I had asthma so bad,

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:26.920
and they would call this
an asthma thing or whatever

00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:31.890
or a cancer thing, I don't
know what to believe anymore,

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:34.030
because I've seen a lot of those doctors

00:13:34.030 --> 00:13:36.880
that were fucking in those
rooms with me that have came

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:40.063
out here, and why are
they in my life like that?

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:42.423
I'll never know.

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:46.730
So I don't know what year
or what age this started

00:13:46.730 --> 00:13:50.320
or when they started doing
this, but I want to say

00:13:50.320 --> 00:13:53.203
it was just five years
ago, but now I don't know.

00:13:57.290 --> 00:14:00.180
You know, I really don't know.
- Are you confused?

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:04.535
- Yeah, why do I have dogs coming out,

00:14:04.535 --> 00:14:06.453
what the fucking shit is this?

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:12.230
Weird shit, ghost shit,

00:14:12.230 --> 00:14:15.950
where I see, like, I call for an angel,

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:18.633
and he brings God of
fucking football angel,

00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:21.883
and I'm just like, where
does that come from?

00:14:23.600 --> 00:14:26.031
You know what I'm saying,
but I'm grateful for it.

00:14:26.031 --> 00:14:28.220
- [Mark] What troubles you the most?

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:29.820
Are you afraid, are you confused?

00:14:29.820 --> 00:14:32.623
- I haven't been able to lay still.

00:14:35.170 --> 00:14:38.893
- Your mind's always moving?
- Just like, nothing in me,

00:14:39.860 --> 00:14:42.650
just that ooh feeling,
you know what I'm saying?

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:47.350
That's what I miss, just
relaxing and not feeling nothing.

00:14:47.350 --> 00:14:50.146
- [Mark] In this neighborhood,
that's impossible.

00:14:50.146 --> 00:14:53.850
- No, just like, every
nerve in my body relaxed

00:14:53.850 --> 00:14:58.593
and not something jumping
out just a little.

00:15:02.070 --> 00:15:04.960
That's what bothers me the most lately,

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:06.490
but other than that, I'm good.

00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:14.190
'Cause they haven't beat me,
they haven't beat nothing.

00:15:14.190 --> 00:15:16.760
Ain't no internal
organs, they already did.

00:15:16.760 --> 00:15:19.700
They hit the brain, brain's gone.

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:22.260
We already determined my brain's gone,

00:15:22.260 --> 00:15:26.508
there's no way in hell
I could have a brain.

00:15:26.508 --> 00:15:29.508
So I'm one of those people that
I don't know, it's just God.

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:35.010
God, and he knew what to
do, because he told me

00:15:35.010 --> 00:15:39.620
these tinkers that were so
big, and I said how do you...

00:15:41.310 --> 00:15:43.000
What the hell do you do?

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:46.760
I said, now I've had it,
I don't even want to know.

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:48.427
Turned out one way,

00:15:48.427 --> 00:15:51.320
and the showed me how
they did it the other day,

00:15:51.320 --> 00:15:56.210
and it was pretty neat,
but yeah, you know,

00:15:56.210 --> 00:16:00.433
stuff like that, so they,
the lies, like, stacked.

00:16:06.430 --> 00:16:07.760
Weirdest shit I've ever seen.

00:16:07.760 --> 00:16:10.323
Whatever he says, I'm with him, you know?

00:16:12.276 --> 00:16:15.253
But I love you, and I'll never stop.

00:16:17.170 --> 00:16:20.600
I thank you for having
you here just sometimes,

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:21.433
you know what I'm saying?

00:16:21.433 --> 00:16:23.130
Just that one little push

00:16:23.130 --> 00:16:26.750
that I do have somebody
else, and you can have

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:28.377
two different friends, you can.

00:16:29.394 --> 00:16:32.476
Who am I to say that you can't?

00:16:32.476 --> 00:16:35.430
That's not me, but just, you know,

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:37.510
don't interfere with my life,
I'm never gonna interfere

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:40.000
with yours, and you can
always come and see me.

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:43.020
I don't care, but then there's some people

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:45.320
that I just don't ever
want to see in my life.

00:16:46.552 --> 00:16:51.552
And I mean that, and I mean
that I'm gonna get you that back

00:16:52.488 --> 00:16:56.383
and when I say that it's
not just me saying that.

00:16:56.383 --> 00:17:00.203
I truly mean that, 'cause
if I can't have a life

00:17:00.203 --> 00:17:03.740
or if I can't have my street
and somebody don't come up

00:17:03.740 --> 00:17:05.250
that knows that I don't want them there,

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:09.280
they're not welcome there, you know?

00:17:09.280 --> 00:17:11.743
And that's where it has went so far.

00:17:15.920 --> 00:17:19.260
- [Mark] Okay, Ruby, thank you
so much for coming in again.

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:20.440
- Yes, sir.

00:17:20.440 --> 00:17:21.360
- [Mark] Always lovely talking to you.

00:17:21.360 --> 00:17:23.573
- Love talking to you too, yes sir.

00:17:25.030 --> 00:17:26.527
- [Mark] Can I buy you some lunch today?

00:17:26.527 --> 00:17:28.460
- Yes, please.
- You got it.

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:29.293
- Yes, sir.

